Here's a JavaScript function that returns a copy of the input array without any duplicates:

```javascript
function removeDuplicates(arr) {
    let uniqueArray = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
        if (uniqueArray.indexOf(arr[i]) === -1) {
            uniqueArray.push(arr[i]);
        }
    }
    return uniqueArray;
}
```

You can call the function with the input array, and it will return the desired output:

```javascript
let inputArray = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 1, 4];
let outputArray = removeDuplicates(inputArray);

console.log(outputArray); // [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
```
